msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/01-architecture.md:1015
#: 78e4f42124594c16a7fd1d86cbb88314
msgid ""
"[Sofia-SIP](https://github.com/freeswitch/sofia-sip) is an LGPL, RFC 3261"
" SIP User-Agent library (Nokia Research Center lineage; FreeSWITCH "
"maintains the fork used here). It is **not** under `libs/`. "
"`configure.ac` requires `sofia-sip-ua >= 1.13.18`. Install/build notes: "
"[Quick Start](../0.getting-started/02-quick-start.md), "
"[FAQ](../7.appendix/02-faq.md). Submodule map: [Tech Stack](02-tech-"
"stack.md#sofia-sip-library)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/01-architecture.md:1017
#: ece741eb670a4ecb932b5debdc707ab1
msgid ""
"`mod_sofia` is the application on top of `libsofia-sip-ua`. One **profile"
" thread** owns one `su_root_t` reactor and one (or more alias) `nua_t` "
"from `nua_create(..., sofia_event_callback, profile, NUTAG_URL(bindurl), "
"...)`. `su_root_step()` waits on tport file descriptors. Inbound bytes "
"become `sip_t` in the library; the first FreeSWITCH symbol is "
"`sofia_event_callback`. That callback clones the event (`nua_save_event`)"
" and hops to a **session** thread (`signal_data_queue`) or the global "
"**MSG** queue so the profile thread can keep reading packets. Packet-"
"level INVITE trace: [Inbound SIP Call](05-workflows.md#inbound-sip-call)."
" NUA/NTA usage, tag lists, and callback rules: [Tech Stack — Sofia-SIP "
"library](02-tech-stack.md#sofia-sip-library)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/01-architecture.md:1019
#: 7aaba9b61bf34a44ba3de69a2efc4b7b
msgid ""
"SIP retransmission timers (`NTATAG_SIP_T1` / `T2` / `T4`) and TCP "
"keepalive tags are Sofia-SIP tport/nta, configured from profile XML in "
"`nua_create`. RTP is **not** Sofia-SIP; it is `switch_rtp` after SDP "
"negotiation."
msgstr ""

